/* (longshot) The hook sites the host gives a flag byte and a callback slot: one line per site of the game's site tables
   (game/sites/sites.toml), included by game/sites.h and game/sites.c with the macros defined there.

     HOS_SITE(<ident>, "<name>")                   a named site nothing in the engine subscribes to: off until hos_site_set()
     HOS_SITE_ENGINE(<ident>, "<name>", <fn>)      a site the engine's own feature uses: on from the start, calling fn
                                                   (int fn(Ctx *A64_NOESC c): its answer read by can_return and branch sites)
     HOS_VALUE(<ident>, "<name>", <type>, <sym>)   a value a data rule reads (rule sites' `value`): the C variable sym,
                                                   volatile, defined by the feature that owns it; hos_value_set writes it
     HOS_TABLE(<ident>, "<name>", <sym>)           a table a data rule reads: const void *volatile sym; hos_table_publish
     HOS_SITE_OUTCOME(<ident>, "<name>")           a site above that changes the game's outcome on a worker thread (branch,
                                                   allow, jump, replace, can_return): no callback set at run time
                                                   (hos_site_add and hos_site_set refuse it); the lift stops when these
                                                   lines are not exactly the table's such sites

   <ident> is the site's name with each dot an underscore (builder/crates/sites ident); the lifted code names hos_site_on_<ident> and
   hos_site_fn_<ident>, so a site in a table with no line here would not link: the lift stops first, naming it
   (builder/crates/sites apply), and builder/crates/sites/tests/repository.rs checks every table against this list. A line for a site no table has (another
   game build's) costs a byte and a pointer. docs/dev/reference/hooks.md has the rest. */

